node_modules/

# The built plugin lives in ../plugin-dist/ and IS committed: it is the artifact a
# user copies into .obsidian/plugins/, and committing it is what lets someone install
# from a clone without a toolchain. It is also what tools/check-invariant.mjs greps —
# a committed bundle means the read-only claim is auditable from the repo alone,
# without trusting that someone's local build matched these sources.

# Local-only oracle capture (see tools/capture-sections.mjs). Nothing here is secret;
# it is machine-specific and regenerated, so it does not belong in git.
test/fixtures/*.local.json

*.log
.DS_Store
